314	<section id="blind">
315	  <h2><span class="num">3</span>The blind rerun</h2>
316	  <p class="gist">At your word the experiment ran again, blind: a new brief that says only what batch 10 must achieve, and two new designers, one on Opus and one on Fable <span class="src">Study</span>.</p>
317	
318	  <div class="sub">
319	    <h3>What its brief held</h3>
320	    <ul>
321	      <li>Three new files, written by a Sonnet worker from batch 10's record <span class="src">Study</span>:
322	        <ul>
323	          <li><code>content.md</code>: the step's aim, its terms, the four <i>pieces</i> W, C, G and N (the rungs under another name) with their defects, files and what done means, who owns which declaration, and the binding decisions, 19 entries quoted from POSITIONS <span class="src">Blind brief</span>;</li>
324	          <li><code>requirements.md</code>: your rules, five of them: test first, both suites green on the merged result, nothing built or run twice, only what <code>main</code> is to hold committed, every language change written into the specification <span class="src">Blind brief</span>;</li>
325	          <li><code>machine.md</code>: the machine and its prices, checked against FACTS <span class="src">Blind brief</span>.</li>
326	        </ul>
327	      </li>
328	      <li>The designers read only that, the source, the specification, the ledger and <code>explorations/repo-internals.md</code> <span class="src">Study</span>. Each design says so in its header <span class="src">Blind Fable header</span> <span class="src">Blind Opus header</span>.</li>
329	    </ul>
