332	  <div class="sub">
333	    <h3>What was removed</h3>
334	    <ul>
335	      <li><b>Every pipeline word</b> <span class="src">Study</span>. None of the three files says rung, skeptic, judge, gather, gate, batch or worker <span class="src">Blind brief</span>.</li>
336	      <li><b>Every past cost</b> <span class="src">Study</span>: no batch 9 cost by stage, no 6M to 7M estimate for batch 10 <span class="src">Rec §1</span>, no "past batches wrote about 6M to 8M" <span class="src">Brief</span>.</li>
337	      <li><b>The record and the files around it.</b> The designers did not open the record, POSITIONS, FACTS or the build-cache note. The brief restates what they need from them.</li>
338	      <li><b>The tier rule.</b> The first brief bound Opus for workers, Sonnet for archaeology, Fable for judgements (section 2). <code>machine.md</code> says only that three tiers exist: Fable the strongest, on its own scarcer weekly pool; Sonnet the cheapest <span class="src">Blind brief</span>.</li>
