426	<section id="designs">
427	  <h2><span class="num">5</span>The four designs</h2>
428	  <p class="gist">The first two keep the pipeline's shape: workers, a checker per rung or pair, one repair round, a merge, one gate; they differ in the checking and in the tail. The blind two have no judge and no review of the merged tree, and differ most in how finely they cut the work.</p>
429	
430	  <div class="sub" id="fable">
431	    <h3>The first Fable design</h3>
432	    <p class="before"><b>Before the launch</b> the coordinator builds the base once, about 4 minutes, and puts each rung's section of the record into the run's arguments <span class="src">Fable §2</span>. <b>Order:</b> C, W, N, G, two at a time <span class="src">Fable §1</span>.</p>
433	    <ol class="roles">
434	      <li>
435	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Worker</span><span class="tier opus">Opus</span><span class="count">×4</span></div>
436	        <p>Its brief is its rung's section of the record, with no separate briefing. Tests first, committed alone. Then one suite run, chosen by what the edit can break: W runs <code>testSystem</code>; C runs the compiler and library tracks of <code>testFast</code>; G and N run only their own tests, which load the whole library. C, G and N run the two stages once at the end. It writes the ledger, FACTS and PLAN lines into its report, not into those files.</p>
437	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>2.5M to 3.3M</b> <span class="src">Fable §4</span></p>
438	      </li>
439	      <li>
440	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Skeptic</span><span class="tier opus">Opus</span><span class="count">×4</span></div>
441	        <p>Reads the git log, the diff, the report and the tool lines of the worker's transcript. Runs 3 to 6 programs of its own on new and old code. Builds nothing. It may refuse only on six listed grounds <span class="src">Fable §2</span>:</p>
442	        <ul>
443	          <li>a test not seen failing first, or not committed alone;</li>
444	          <li>a stop of the brief met and not listed;</li>
445	          <li>a fix against the text or library practice the brief cites;</li>
446	          <li>a file touched outside the brief's list;</li>
447	          <li>a value changed without the brief's warrant;</li>
448	          <li>a test that cannot fail for the reason it names.</li>
449	        </ul>
450	        <p>Anything else is a note for you.</p>
451	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.8M to 1.2M</b>, 0.2M to 0.3M each <span class="src">Fable §4</span></p>
452	      </li>
453	      <li>
454	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">After a refusal</span><span class="count">one chain expected</span></div>
455	        <ul>
456	          <li><span class="tier opus">Opus</span> <b>Repair</b> of exactly the named grounds: 0.3M.</li>
457	          <li><span class="tier opus">Opus</span> <b>Second read</b>, of those grounds only: 0.15M.</li>
458	          <li><span class="tier opus">Opus</span> <b>Ruling</b>, only if the second read refuses again, approve or drop: 0.15M.</li>
459	          <li><span class="tier fable">Fable</span> <b>Second ruling</b>, only if the Opus ruling says the dispute is a design question across two of the specification, the library and the implementation: 0.15M, rarely.</li>
460	        </ul>
461	        <p>A rung not approved stays on its branch; the batch lands without it.</p>
462	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.6M</b> a chain; one expected, two budgeted <span class="src">Fable §4</span></p>
463	      </li>
464	      <li>
465	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Gather</span><span class="tier opus">Opus</span></div>
466	        <p>Merges the approved branches with merge commits in a seeded worktree, and writes the records from the workers' reports.</p>
467	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.25M</b> <span class="src">Fable §4</span></p>
468	      </li>
469	      <li>
470	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Gate</span><span class="tier sonnet">Sonnet, low effort</span></div>
471	        <p>One build of the merged tree, then <code>testFast</code>, <code>testSystem</code>, the ladder, the count and the distance, one after another. A red gate gets one Opus repair and one more gate.</p>
472	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.10M to 0.15M</b>; a red gate adds 0.4M and 0.1M, expected once in three batches <span class="src">Fable §4</span></p>
473	      </li>
474	      <li>
475	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Landing</span><span class="tier sonnet">Sonnet, low effort</span></div>
476	        <p>Writes the gate's numbers into the landing note, fast-forwards <code>main</code>, pushes, starts the microGPT runs.</p>
477	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.08M</b> <span class="src">Fable §4</span></p>
478	      </li>
479	    </ol>
480	    <p class="note">Not in it: the merged-diff review, and a judge on every refusal <span class="src">Fable §1</span>.</p>
481	    <div class="total">
482	      <p><b>Estimate:</b> about 5.2M (4.3M to 6.8M), including about 0.25M of the coordinator's own work outside the run. 11 to 19 agents, 13 to 14 expected. About 9 to 10 hours <span class="src">Fable §4</span>.</p>
483	    </div>
484	  </div>
