486	  <div class="sub" id="opus">
487	    <h3>The first Opus design</h3>
488	    <p class="before"><b>Before the launch</b> the coordinator builds or reuses the base build, renders each rung's briefing, and commits two small tools: <code>gate.sh</code>, the gate's steps as one script, and <code>test-first-trace.py</code>, which prints a worker's test runs from its transcript <span class="src">Opus §2, §5</span>. <b>Order:</b> C, N, G, W, two at a time <span class="src">Opus §1</span>.</p>
489	    <ol class="roles">
490	      <li>
491	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Worker</span><span class="tier opus">Opus</span><span class="count">×4</span></div>
492	        <p>Its rung's section plus its briefing. Tests first, committed alone; the fix; the text in the S1 form. One <i>reach run</i>, the part of the suite its change can reach: <code>testFast</code> for C, <code>testSystem</code> for W, N and G. C, N and G run the two stages once. New ledger rows get placeholders that the integrator numbers.</p>
493	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>2.25M</b> (1.8M to 2.75M) <span class="src">Opus §4</span></p>
494	      </li>
495	      <li>
496	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Checker</span><span class="tier opus">Opus</span><span class="count">×3</span></div>
497	        <p>One for W, one for C, and one for N and G together. Checks test first from git and the transcript, the paths touched, each fix against its text or precedent, at most eight programs of its own, the worker's results, and the revised text <span class="src">Opus §2</span>. It may commit text-only corrections. It approves unless a code or test finding stands on a program or a cited line.</p>
498	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.88M</b> (0.69M to 1.12M) <span class="src">Opus §4</span></p>
499	      </li>
500	      <li>
501	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">After a refusal</span><span class="count">1.4 expected</span></div>
502	        <ul>
503	          <li><span class="tier opus">Opus</span> <b>Repair</b>: accepts each finding, turning the checker's program into a test that fails first and then fixing it, or contests it with evidence. About 0.28M each, 0.43M expected.</li>
504	          <li><span class="tier fable">Fable</span> <b>Ruling</b>, only for a contested finding: one ruling, final. About 0.15M each, 0.05M expected.</li>
505	          <li><span class="tier opus">Opus</span> <b>Second repair</b>, only after an upheld ruling: 0.04M expected.</li>
506	        </ul>
507	        <p>No second skeptic.</p>
508	        <p class="cost">Estimates <span class="src">Opus §4</span></p>
509	      </li>
510	      <li>
511	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Integrator</span><span class="tier opus">Opus</span></div>
512	        <p>Merges with merge commits into a fresh, unseeded worktree, numbers the rows, starts <code>gate.sh</code> in the background (a clean build and the full gate, 25 to 35 minutes <span class="src">Opus §2</span>), and writes the records while it runs. Pushes a work branch, never <code>main</code>.</p>
513	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.28M</b> <span class="src">Opus §4</span></p>
514	      </li>
515	      <li>
516	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Reviewer</span><span class="tier opus">Opus</span><span class="count">beside the integrator</span></div>
517	        <p>Reads the four diffs side by side for what no single check could see. Its text corrections land before the push. Its code findings become rows for the next batch and block nothing.</p>
518	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.25M</b> <span class="src">Opus §4</span></p>
519	      </li>
520	      <li>
521	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Gate repair</span><span class="tier opus">Opus</span><span class="count">red gate only</span></div>
522	        <p>Repairs the merged tree as a whole, then one more gate.</p>
523	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.1M</b> expected (0.4M at a 0.25 chance) <span class="src">Opus §4</span></p>
524	      </li>
525	      <li>
526	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Lander</span><span class="tier opus">Opus, low effort</span></div>
527	        <p>Applies the review's text corrections, checks that no gated path changed since the gate, pushes <code>main</code>, starts the microGPT runs.</p>
528	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.08M</b> <span class="src">Opus §4</span></p>
529	      </li>
530	      <li>
531	        <div class="role-head"><span class="role-name">Measure</span><span class="tier sonnet">Sonnet, low effort</span></div>
532	        <p>Measures the run's cost by role from its journal and writes it beside this estimate.</p>
533	        <p class="cost">Estimate: <b>0.1M</b> <span class="src">Opus §4</span></p>
534	      </li>
535	    </ol>
536	    <div class="total">
537	      <p><b>Estimate:</b> about 4.3M on Opus (3.0M to 6.4M), up to 0.2M on Fable, about 0.1M on Sonnet. 10 Opus agents and the measure in the base case, about 12 expected, 17 at worst. About 9.5 to 10 hours (8 to 12) <span class="src">Opus §4</span>.</p>
538	    </div>
539	  </div>
